Hi!

 

I'm participating in small science project, that consist in centos-base
kernel development. 

One of the goals is regression testing of memory management from one version
to another. And some autotesting system would be a great helpful for this.

I found kernelci.org in web and after reading howto's have several
questions:

1.       Could I install kernelCi on local computer(s) so, that it builds
and tests our  kernel? I think we can't maintain actual lab, on the other
hand testing in remote lab may be  time-consuming due to coordination exps.

2.       Could I add some new tests in testplan and what should I do for
this?

 

Regards, 

Dmitry Moskalev.


